{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed a stalled order pipeline and submitted the mitigation. The submission returned 200. I haven't confirmed end-user request success or latency myself, and I never established that this stall was the cause of the degraded service.\n\n- **Cause:** `orders-validator` (the Kafka consumer on `orders-fulfillment`) stopped at offset 20 after one record failed JSON parsing. The original code then paused indefinitely, so nothing after that record was processed.\n- **Fix:** I edited the consumer script in the `orders-pipeline-scripts` ConfigMap. A bad record now goes to a dead-letter topic (`orders-processed-dlq`), its offset is committed, and the consumer moves on. I restarted `orders-validator`.\n- **Result:** The consumer is processing again and had reached offset 49 at last check. All pods in `astronomy-shop` were Running. I didn't check metrics or traces for the other services.\n\nThe `frontend` logs showed gRPC connection errors at startup. They were from before the services came up, and I didn't look into them further."}}
